# Private project-name denylist — TEMPLATE (placeholders only).
#
# This file is safe to commit: it contains NO real names. The real denylist is
# DATA and must live OUTSIDE this public repo, or the guard leaks the very names
# it protects.
#
# WHERE THE REAL FILE LIVES:
#   Canonical copy is checked in PRIVATELY in a separate private fleet repo
#   (durable, documented, version-controlled — but never public). Distribute it
#   to public repos by symlinking it one level up, into ~/coding:
#
#     ln -s ~/coding/<private-fleet-repo>/path/to/fleet-private-refs ~/coding/fleet-private-refs
#
#   check-private-refs.sh then resolves it, first-existing-wins:
#     1. $PRIVATE_NAMES_FILE                        (explicit override; CI)
#     2. ~/.config/tracepulse/fleet-private-refs    (absolute fallback)
#     3. <repo>/../fleet-private-refs               (the ~/coding symlink above)
#
# ALTERNATIVE bootstrap (no symlink) — copy to the absolute path:
#     mkdir -p ~/.config/tracepulse
#     cp scripts/private-names.example ~/.config/tracepulse/fleet-private-refs
#     # then replace the placeholders below with the real names.
#
# Format: one name per line, case-insensitive match, '#' starts a comment.

example-app-one
example-app-two
example-service
